Exercise 5: Undo Changes Using Git Commands
AIM: To undo unwanted file changes using Git commands such as git checkout, git reset, and git
revert.
ALGORITHM
STEP 1: Open a terminal.
STEP 2: Navigate to the Git repository.
STEP 3: Create and commit a file containing original content.
STEP 4: Modify the file to demonstrate an unwanted change.
STEP 5: Use git restore to discard an unstaged change.
STEP 6: Use git reset or git revert when appropriate to undo committed changes.
STEP 7: Check the repository status and verify the result.
STEP 8: End the terminal.
TERMINAL RUN CODE
cd git-practical
echo &quot;Original content&quot; &gt; undo-demo.txt
git add undo-demo.txt
git commit -m &quot;Add original content&quot;

echo &quot;Unwanted change&quot; &gt; undo-demo.txt
git restore undo-demo.txt
cat undo-demo.txt
git status

