Exercise 7: Resolve a Merge Conflict
AIM: To identify and resolve a merge conflict between two Git branches.
ALGORITHM
STEP 1: Open a terminal.
STEP 2: Navigate to the Git repository.
STEP 3: Create a new branch for the conflicting changes.
STEP 4: Modify the same file on the new branch and commit the change.
STEP 5: Switch to the main branch and modify the same file differently.
STEP 6: Commit the main branch change.
STEP 7: Merge the feature branch into the main branch.
STEP 8: Identify the merge conflict and edit the file to retain the required content.
STEP 9: Stage the resolved file and commit the merge resolution.
STEP 10: Verify the final file content and end the terminal.
TERMINAL RUN CODE
The following is a sample demonstration. Start with a clean repository and use a separate practice
file.
cd git-practical
echo &quot;Welcome to Git&quot; &gt; conflict-demo.txt
git add conflict-demo.txt
git commit -m &quot;Add conflict demo file&quot;

git switch -c feature-conflict
echo &quot;Feature branch content&quot; &gt; conflict-demo.txt
git add conflict-demo.txt
git commit -m &quot;Update file in feature branch&quot;

git switch main
echo &quot;Main branch content&quot; &gt; conflict-demo.txt
git add conflict-demo.txt
git commit -m &quot;Update file in main branch&quot;

