STEP 4: Navigate into the cloned repository.
STEP 5: Create a file containing sample content.
STEP 6: Stage and commit the file.
STEP 7: Push the commit to GitHub using git push.
STEP 8: Pull the latest remote changes using git pull.
STEP 9: Verify the file and repository status.
STEP 10: End the terminal.
TERMINAL RUN CODE
Use a different folder name if git-practical already exists in your current directory.
cd /workspaces
git clone https://github.com/anandajothi-2007/git-practical.git
cd git-practical
